    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      A captive-air well pressure tank uses a flexible butyl rubber diaphragm to separate stored potable water from a pressurized air cushion. Because water is an incompressible fluid, the air cushion acts as an elastic spring that pushes water through your house pipes without requiring the deep-well pump to start every time someone washes their hands. To maintain seamless water delivery and protect the submersible pump motor, you must calibrate the dry air pre-charge to <strong>precisely 2 PSI below the pressure switch cut-in setting</strong>.
    </p>

